---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="AITS was built differently — on 25+ years of onboarding, integrating, deploying, and managing technology that has to keep working. One flat fee. Fixes included."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="section-label">About AITS</p>
      <h1>We do things differently. From the ground up.</h1>
      <p>
        AITS — Advanced Intelligent Technology Solutions — helps small and mid-sized businesses
        put AI to work so they compete with companies five times their size. But we were not built
        like most AI companies. We were built on 25+ years of onboarding, integrating, deploying,
        and managing software, hardware, and full solutions — through every era of business
        technology: the first office servers, the rise of the cloud, and everything in between.
        AI is our newest tool. It is not our first rodeo.
      </p>

      <h2>The week-three problem — and why we exist.</h2>
      <p>
        Here is what we watched happen again and again: a business buys an AI solution, and it
        works beautifully on day one. Then week two or three arrives. One of the tools underneath
        pushes an update, a connection quietly breaks, and nobody on the team knows how to fix it.
        So they call the company that built it — and get billed. Every single time. That vendor's
        business model profits when things break.
      </p>
      <p>
        AITS is the inverse. One flat monthly fee covers the tools <em>and</em> the team that keeps
        them working: every automation tested on a regular schedule, uptime monitored continuously,
        and fixes included. Every "it's broken" call costs us, not you — so our whole incentive is
        to make sure you never have to make one. That is what 25 years of managing technology
        teaches you: day one is easy. Month three is the difference.
      </p>

      <h2>A partnership that grows with you.</h2>
      <p>
        This is a true business partnership, not a transaction. As your company grows, you will
        need more automation to keep your team focused on the work that drives revenue — not the
        busywork pulling them away from it. We grow with you: adding services, expanding
        automations, and finding the next hours to hand back to your people. Your growth is our
        roadmap.
      </p>

      <h2>We do not run pilots. We deliver results.</h2>
      <p>
        Every engagement starts with an early win your entire team can see and feel. We start with
        the tasks your team hates most, automate those first, and make sure every person sees the
        benefit before we touch anything else. That is how adoption sticks — and adoption is where
        most AI deployments quietly fail.
      </p>

      <h2>Built by a next-generation founder. Backed by decades of real-world results.</h2>
      <p>
        {BUSINESS.founder} launched AITS with the vision and energy of a builder who grew up inside
        the technology industry. Behind him stands a board with over 80 combined years of managed
        services, AI deployment, and business leadership across North America — the same people
        whose operational discipline is built into how AITS runs every client's technology.
      </p>

      <h2>In your corner, wherever you are.</h2>
      <p>
        AITS is headquartered in San Diego and serves businesses across the entire United States.
        In Southern California we can be on-site when something needs a human — everywhere else,
        you get the same team, the same platform, and the same response when something needs
        attention. And we work month-to-month: you stay because the results justify it.
      </p>

      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Get your free AI assessment</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin: 12px 0 24px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
  }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .btn {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
</style>
